1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,000
This is a SAANJH-enabled neighbourhood distribution network.

2
00:00:05,000 --> 00:00:10,000
It is currently operating within normal parameters.

3
00:00:10,000 --> 00:00:17,000
We are looking at 60 individual households. 66% are equipped with rooftop solar and battery storage.

4
00:00:25,000 --> 00:00:32,000
During the afternoon, solar generation meets local demand, keeping feeder stress low.

5
00:00:40,000 --> 00:00:48,000
As evening approaches, solar declines, and residential demand naturally increases.

6
00:00:55,000 --> 00:01:05,000
The SAANJH predictive engine detects an impending anomaly: the feeder will exceed its thermal rating.

7
00:01:10,000 --> 00:01:20,000
The Edge Gateway aggregates available flexibility into a single Virtual Battery via LoRa.

8
00:01:30,000 --> 00:01:40,000
The stress event arrives. Selected homes intelligently discharge to dynamically compensate.

9
00:01:45,000 --> 00:01:55,000
Observe the transformer stress visualization. The injected flexibility drops peak demand back to a safe band.

10
00:01:55,000 --> 00:02:00,000
As the peak subsides, homes enter a staggered recovery phase.

11
00:02:00,000 --> 00:02:10,000
Final metrics confirm SAANJH successfully mitigated the overload without expensive hardware upgrades.

12
00:02:10,000 --> 00:02:16,000
SAANJH: Securing the edge, one neighbourhood at a time.
